Privately Attack Chains =E2=80=94 defensive synthesis

1 NEW ATTACK CHAINS

AC-2026-SHARED-HARNESS-AUTHORITY =E2=80=94 LAB/RECENT

Canonical fingerprint: shared agent harness/config -> scoped-looking
permission grant -> inherited pre-approval -> arbitrary execution
authority -> credential/tool/cloud access UNKNOWN -> external
privileged action UNKNOWN.

A September 2026 empirical study of 3,171 public AI coding-agent
configurations reported three validated security classes: 9.8%
installed an unpinned MCP server, 3.1% pre-approved arbitrary
execution behind apparently scoped grants such as interpreter-specific
shell permissions, and 3.8% contained skills that pre-approved shell
execution for installers.

Stages/edges: shared skill/config [CONFIRMED] -> installation into
agent harness [CONFIRMED] -> inherited pre-approval [CONFIRMED] ->
arbitrary local execution authority [CONFIRMED] ->
credential/tool/cloud access [UNKNOWN] -> external privileged action
[UNKNOWN]. Researchers did not establish a confirmed
credential-exfiltration path, so later edges remain UNKNOWN.

2 MATERIAL CHAIN UPDATES

The existing trust-order / authority-inheritance cluster is
strengthened by GitSpawn: repository-controlled Git configuration can
cause commands to execute as the developer, outside the agent sandbox
and in affected agents before intended trust/authentication
boundaries.

3 TOP RECURRING SECOND-ORDER MECHANISMS

Configuration that appears descriptive or narrowly scoped can acquire
execution authority before, or independently of, the intended human
approval boundary.

4 STAGE/EDGE GRAPH

repository/shared config -> agent harness -> inherited permission ->
execution authority -> [UNKNOWN secret/session] -> [UNKNOWN external
action]

5 UNKNOWN LINKS WORTH RESOLVING

Highest-value missing link: pre-approved harness execution ->
secret/session access -> delegated external action.

6 DEFENSIVE CHOKEPOINTS

Install-time capability analysis; immutable/version-pinned MCP
identities; explicit denial of transitive permission inheritance;
agent/editor configuration-change detection; no repository-derived
configuration execution before workspace trust.

7 SAFE LAB REPRODUCTION

Disposable repository and dummy environment variable. Test whether a
narrowly presented permission can trigger a benign local marker write.
No real credentials or external targets.

8 CROSS-CASE CLUSTER

Trust-order / authority-inheritance: repository configuration, agent
harness permissions, and pre-trust execution surfaces.

